---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { rtiReplies } from '../../data/rti-replies';
---
<Base title="RTI replies" description="What government bodies told AVI, under the Right to Information Act, about the research behind India's e-cigarette ban — organised by department, not a raw document scroll." wide={true}>
  <section class="breakout rti-hero">
    <div class="breakout-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Right to Information, 2018–2019</p>
      <h1>What government departments actually told us — on the record</h1>
      <p class="rti-sub">
        The Right to Information Act, 2005 lets any Indian citizen formally
        request records from a public authority; the authority's Public
        Information Officer (CPIO) is legally required to respond. Concerned
        about the government's hard line on e-cigarettes, AVI and individual
        vapers filed RTI requests with the research bodies, health ministry
        and customs authorities most likely to have studied the issue —
        asking a simple question: what evidence was this policy actually
        based on?
      </p>
      <p class="rti-sub">
        The replies below, grouped by department, show a consistent pattern:
        no research had been conducted, no budget existed for it, and — from
        India's own drug regulators and customs authorities — e-cigarettes
        were, at the time, not covered by the law later cited to restrict
        them. Each card shows what was asked, what was said, and a link to
        the original reply.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="rti-body">
    <div class="rti-grid">
      {rtiReplies.map((r) => (
        <article class="rti-card">
          <div class="card-top">
            <Icon name="document" />
          </div>
          <h2>{r.authority}</h2>
          <p class="jurisdiction">{r.jurisdiction}</p>

          <div class="qa-block">
            <h3>Asked</h3>
            <ul class="questions">
              {r.questions.map((q) => <li>{q}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="qa-block">
            <h3>Replied</h3>
            <ul class="findings">
              {r.findings.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>

          {r.localFile
            ? <a class="read-link" href={r.localFile} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the original reply →</a>
            : <a class="read-link external" href={r.driveUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the original reply (opens in Google Drive) →</a>}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="rti-footnote">
      Several questions above were asked in near-identical, redundant
      phrasing across the original set of RTI applications (e.g. "electronic
      cigarettes" vs. "electronic vaping devices" vs. "ENDS") — they're
      consolidated here to one entry per underlying question. Five of the
      eleven original reply documents could not be re-hosted on this site
      directly and link out to Google Drive instead; everything else is
      archived locally so it won't disappear if that link ever does.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--gold-dark);
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }
    .rti-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(rgba(18,19,15,0.85), rgba(18,19,15,0.93)), url('/images/backgrounds/open-sky.jpg');
      background-size: cover;
      background-position: center;
      color: #f4f1e6;
      padding: 3.5rem 0 3rem;
    }
    .rti-hero h1 { color: #fff; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem); max-width: 46rem; }
    .rti-sub { color: #cdd6cf; max-width: 44rem; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .rti-sub:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .rti-body { max-width: var(--max-w-wide); margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .rti-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(21rem, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .rti-card {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.6rem;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(20,25,20,0.05);
      border-top: 4px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .card-top :global(svg) { width: 1.4rem; height: 1.4rem; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
    .rti-card h2 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.35; }
    .jurisdiction { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }

    .qa-block { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .qa-block h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--gold-dark);
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .qa-block ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.87rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    .qa-block li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
    .qa-block li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .findings li { color: var(--ink); }
    .questions li { color: var(--muted); }

    .read-link { font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-dark); margin-top: auto; padding-top: 0.5rem; }
    .read-link.external { color: var(--gold-dark); }

    .rti-footnote {
      max-width: 44rem;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding-top: 1.5rem;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
